---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="The Morning Build is a free daily briefing on the AI and tech stories that matter to people who build. Read it in just a few minutes."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="digest">
      <h1>The day's tech news, without the hours of scrolling.</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Keeping up with AI and tech is a job in itself. New models, new
          tools, new chips, new rules, every single day. Reading it all takes
          hours you don't have. Skipping it means falling behind.
        </p>
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} is the fix: one short briefing every morning with the
          handful of stories that actually matter to people who build.
        </p>

        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A new briefing every morning</li>
          <li>The handful of stories that matter, nothing else</li>
          <li>For each one: what happened, why it matters, what to watch next</li>
          <li>Read the whole thing in just a few minutes</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each briefing links to its source reporting, so you can read the
          original coverage and check the context.
        </p>

        <h2>How this is made</h2>
        <p>
          An automated pipeline selects stories and uses AI to write summaries
          and analysis. Briefings are published without a human editorial review
          step. Automated checks do not guarantee factual accuracy; consult the
          linked sources before relying on a claim.
        </p>
        <p>
          “Outlook” is AI-generated interpretation of what may happen next,
          not independently verified reporting or a prediction you can rely on.
          To report an error or request a correction,
          <a href="https://github.com/noetion/digest/issues/new">open an issue</a>
          with the briefing URL and supporting source.
        </p>

        <h2>How to read it</h2>
        <p>
          A new briefing lands here every morning. Read it with your coffee,
          or point your feed reader at <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a> or
          <a href="/atom.xml">Atom</a> and the full briefing comes to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Start your morning here.
          <a href="/">Read today's briefing &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
